(7593971, 1224797, 114285, '<td valign="top">I can see this on a wall, the best of the created smoke images.</td>', 'I can see this on a wall, the best of the created smoke images.', '2018-08-27 05:12:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(7594198, 1224903, 87808, '<td valign="top">SO clean and crisp, nicely done!</td>', 'SO clean and crisp, nicely done!', '2018-08-28 14:18:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(7594199, 1224887, 87808, '<td valign="top">SO very close!!! the photo is tilted though and make your head tilt to compensate. In standard editing,  you can get that paint brush and put it on white with maybe a 20% and paint that smoke, so that it stands out more,. Or you could dodge it a little. Also , something I do, is I hold my hands up, side by side look at a photo through my hands to see if there would be a better crop.  I think if you cropped it in-between those outer plants directly on that white ''chair"(?) on the right hand side and just after that white/red pillar on the left, you would have had a good crop and more dramatic photo. Also, I am seeing, blue in teh sky at the middle of your photo, but then very grey at the left and right hand top sides. If you use a gradient filter set to blue(ish) you would have a great colour for the sky and it would increase teh colour in the  upper building.</td>', 'SO very close!!! the photo is tilted though and make your head tilt to compensate. In standard editing,  you can get that paint brush and put it on white with maybe a 20% and paint that smoke, so that it stands out more,. Or you could dodge it a little. Also , something I do, is I hold my hands up, side by side look at a photo through my hands to see if there would be a better crop.  I think if you cropped it in-between those outer plants directly on that white ''chair"(?) on the right hand side and just after that white/red pillar on the left, you would have had a good crop and more dramatic photo. Also, I am seeing, blue in teh sky at the middle of your photo, but then very grey at the left and right hand top sides. If you use a gradient filter set to blue(ish) you would have a great colour for the sky and it would increase teh colour in the  upper building.', '2018-08-28 14:19:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(7594200, 1224861, 87808, '<td valign="top">This is a great photo!!  I would love to see this in BW with a ton of contrast to really make that smoke and brickwork pop, I think it would have a much more visceral impact on viewers. For myself, personally, I could then image I was on the steam train (not the Orient Express) that Hercule Poirot was on, ((eating miniature watercress sandwiches and complaining that the coal dust is settling on his suit)), traveling back to London, after a grand adventure. So much ore drama could be added to this. It is fabulous that you got to shoot something that most people never experience!</td>', 'This is a great photo!!  I would love to see this in BW with a ton of contrast to really make that smoke and brickwork pop, I think it would have a much more visceral impact on viewers. For myself, personally, I could then image I was on the steam train (not the Orient Express) that Hercule Poirot was on, ((eating miniature watercress sandwiches and complaining that the coal dust is settling on his suit)), traveling back to London, after a grand adventure. So much ore drama could be added to this. It is fabulous that you got to shoot something that most people never experience!', '2018-08-28 14:20:42.000000', NULL, 1),
